  "problem": "A certain company produces three types of milk: whole, skim, and lactose-free. The following table describes how the number of customers changes between the three types of milk each year:\n\n|  |  | From: |  |  |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- | --- |\n|  |  | **Whole** | **Skim** | **Lactose-free** |\n| To: | **Whole** | $0.5$ | $0.3$ | $0.2$ |\n| **Skim** | $0.3$ | $0.4$ | $0.4$ |  |\n| **Lactose-free** | $0.2$ | $0.3$ | $0.4$ |  |\n\nFor example, $30%$ of whole milk customers switch to skim milk each year, and $20%$ of lactose-free milk customers switch to whole milk.\n\nCurrently, $400\\,000$ customers consume whole milk, $400\\,000$ customers consume skim milk, and $200\\,000$ customers consume lactose-free milk. How many customers will consume whole milk after one year? You may assume that the total number of customers doesn't change.",
